      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- **II.** $T$ is a singular matrix\n\n- **III.** $det(T)=\\frac{32}{3}$\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 4 \\\\ - \\frac{4}{3} & - \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
